    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Kyle Tucker** (77.08) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.85), who emerge as our premier plays against favorable matchups. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a robust 4.79 xERA opponent in Brandon Young, allowing his high base projection to shine without the need for significant platoon adjustments. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in an ideal spot against Nick Martinez; his 14% boost from a dynamic platoon edge, combined with an aggressive #2 spot in the order, elevates his efficiency score well into the elite tier. **Andy Pages** also draws the same advantageous matchup against Young, capitalizing on a clean neutral platoon split to provide secondary support in the outfield with a 72.55 score.\n\nWhile our core lineup is optimized, the most difficult decision was keeping **Nasim Nunez** (51.42) on the bench. Despite his role as a critical speed specialist\u2014essential in our pursuit of the scarce stolen base category\u2014his placement in the #9 hole carries an 8% penalty that suppresses his total utility below the threshold required to displace starters like **Jacob Wilson** or **Curtis Mead**. We must also monitor the status of **Nolan Schanuel** and **Gunnar Henderson**, as both carry \"Lineup Pending\" designations. Should **Nolan Schanuel** be dropped from the #2 spot upon the official release, we will lose the 8% order bonus that currently anchors his 57.82 score. **Jacob Wilson** presents the highest risk today, facing Reid Detmers\u2019 3.23 xERA; while his 54.18 score is sufficient for a start, he is the most susceptible to an efficiency drop if the left-on-left dynamic does not break our way.",
